  "notes": "Post-Wallen rock-country — screamed-edge tenor, half-time trap-rock drums, minor keys. The catalogue's fingerprint is unusually legible and is authored as stated: \"a ~73–85 spine with the backbeat on 2&4 (songdata's recurring 146/170/183 readings are doubled values of ~73/85/91), plus true midtempos at 107–135,\" and \"F♯ major dominates his catalogue to a striking degree (the majority of his album cuts read F♯ or A).\" So F♯ carries the top key weight and the band centres at 80 despite reaching 135. Drums are \"programmed clap/snap backbeat, 16th hats with rolls, short sampled kicks, big reverbed rock snare on the final chorus, and full drop-outs before choruses\" — hence the clap layer, the roll set and the highest drop-out figure of the 2020s cohort here. The 808 is `counter_riff` because both layers are named: \"tuned 808-style sub as the low end, long and root-locked, with slides into section downbeats; a distorted electric bass doubles it on the rock cuts.\" Harmony is \"I–V–vi–IV and i–VI–III–VII as two-bar loops over a static sub,\" which is the `2_bars_per_chord` weighting and only two families carrying real weight. Melody is \"high tenor pushed to the edge of the register with rasp and cracked notes, long sustained chorus peaks, and pitched vocal doubles as texture\" — the highest male register in the modern half of this section. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: medium-high, with the key and tempo concentrations called \"unusually clear\"); the per-track readings still carry the section's [LOW-CONF] class mark. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the 808 register, the perc density and the counter ratio.",
